# 1. Insertion at First

A new node is inserted **before the current head**.

## Cases

### Case 1: `head == NULL`

The linked list is empty.

```text
Before:

head → NULL

Insert 10

After:

head
 ↓
10 → NULL
```

### Case 2: Nodes Already Exist

```text
Before:

head
 ↓
10 → 20 → 30 → NULL

Insert 5

After:

head
 ↓
5 → 10 → 20 → 30 → NULL
```

### Main Logic

```cpp
temp->next = head;
head = temp;
```

### Code

```cpp
void insertAtFirst(int data)
{
    Node *temp = new Node(data);

    temp->next = head;
    head = temp;
}
```

---

# 2. Insertion at Last

A new node is inserted **at the end** of the linked list.

There are **2 cases**.

## Case 1: `head == NULL`

The linked list is empty.

```text
Before:

head → NULL

Insert 10

After:

head
 ↓
10 → NULL
```

### Logic

```cpp
head = temp;
return;
```

---

## Case 2: `n > 0` Nodes

Suppose the linked list already contains nodes.

```text
Before:

head
 ↓
10 → 20 → 30 → NULL

Insert 40

After:

head
 ↓
10 → 20 → 30 → 40 → NULL
```

### Find the Last Node

```cpp
while (temp->next != NULL)
{
    temp = temp->next;
}

temp->next = newNode;
```

### Code

```cpp
void insertAtLast(int data)
{
    Node *newNode = new Node(data);

    // Case 1: No node
    if (head == NULL)
    {
        head = newNode;
        return;
    }

    // Case 2: n nodes
    Node *temp = head;

    while (temp->next != NULL)
    {
        temp = temp->next;
    }

    temp->next = newNode;
}
```

---

# 3. Insertion in Between

Insert a new node **after a targeted value**.

There are **3 cases**.

## Case 1: List is Empty

```text
head → NULL

"No nodes are there"
```

### Code

```cpp
if (head == NULL)
{
    cout << "Nodes are not there" << endl;
    return;
}
```

---

## Case 2: Target Not Found

Suppose:

```text
10 → 20 → 30 → NULL

Target = 50
```

Since `50` is not present:

```text
"Targeted node doesn't exist"
```

### Code

```cpp
if (temp == NULL)
{
    cout << "Targeted node doesn't exist" << endl;
    return;
}
```

---

## Case 3: Target Found

Suppose the target is `20`.

```text
Before:

10 → 20 → 30 → NULL
      ↑
    target
```

Insert `25`.

```text
After:

10 → 20 → 25 → 30 → NULL
```

### Main Logic

```cpp
newNode->next = temp->next;
temp->next = newNode;
```

### Code

```cpp
void insertInBetween(int data, int targetedValue)
{
    // Case 1: No node
    if (head == NULL)
    {
        cout << "Nodes are not there" << endl;
        return;
    }

    Node *temp = head;

    // Find target
    while (temp != NULL &&
           temp->value != targetedValue)
    {
        temp = temp->next;
    }

    // Case 2: Target not found
    if (temp == NULL)
    {
        cout << "Targeted node doesn't exist" << endl;
        return;
    }

    // Case 3: Target found
    Node *newNode = new Node(data);

    newNode->next = temp->next;
    temp->next = newNode;
}
```

---

# 4. Display / Traversal

Display means visiting every node from `head` to `NULL`.

```text
head
 ↓
10 → 20 → 25 → 30 → NULL
```

### Code

```cpp
void display()
{
    if (head == NULL)
    {
        cout << "No nodes exist" << endl;
        return;
    }

    Node *temp = head;

    while (temp != NULL)
    {
        cout << temp->value << " ";
        temp = temp->next;
    }

    cout << endl;
}
```

